row(19, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'BURNED BEFORE HIS EYES — SKIN, FLESH, BLOOD, ON ITS DUNG. "{H(19, 5, "ושרף", "את", "הפרה", "לעיניו")}" ("and one shall burn the heifer before his eyes" — the burn-verb\'s consonants are 17:4\'s "the BURNT ones" and 21:6\'s "the FIERY serpents"; computed) → {A(19, 5, "ויוקד", "ית", "תורתא", "לעינוהי")} ("and one shall burn the cow before his eyes"); "{H(19, 5, "את", "ערה", "ואת", "בשרה", "ואת", "דמה", "על", "פרשה", "ישרף")}" ("its skin and its flesh and its blood on its dung shall he burn" — one seat: THE SIN-BULL\'S BURN-LIST (Exod 29:14, Lev 4:11, 16:27: skin, flesh, dung) WITH THE BLOOD ADDED — the Sifrei\'s "any blood left is returned or the heifer is invalid", 124:1; computed on the three lists) → {A(19, 5, "ית", "משכה", "וית", "בשרה", "וית", "דמה", "על", "אכלה", "יוקד")} ("its skin and its flesh and its blood on ITS FOOD shall he burn" — the dung rendered as what it ate, cut from the shelf\'s bytes).')
